      "side": 1,
      "message": "The race condition I see is as follows:\n* A SCSI command is submitted and gets past the check of whether or not SCSI command processing is blocked. The ufshcd_queuecommand() call for that command has not yet happened.\n* ufshcd_get_exclusive_access() waits until the TMF and SCSI command doorbells are zero.\n* ufshcd_queuecommand() is called and submits the SCSI command while a keyslot is being reprogrammed.\n\nThe above race could not happen as long as ufshcd_queuecommand() obtained the clk_scaling_lock. This race can happen today since the code to grab the clk_scaling_lock has been removed from ufshcd_queuecommand(). This race is addressed by calling ufshcd_wait_for_doorbell_clr() and because that function checks for SCSI commands by calling ufshcd_pending_cmds(). That last function checks SCSI state information that is updated before the \"host blocked\" check happens.",
